      "text": "The error happens because the qasm simulator only stores counts by default, so `get_statevector` has nothing to return. The fix is to add a save-statevector instruction to the circuit.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, execute\nfrom qiskit.providers.aer import QasmSimulator\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(2)\nqc.h(0)\nqc.cx(0, 1)\n# FIX: no statevector was saved in the circuit -> added qc.save_statevector(), because QasmSimulator only returns data from explicit save instructions, so get_statevector fails without it\nqc.save_statevector()\n\nbackend = QasmSimulator()\nbackend_options = {\"method\": \"statevector\"}\n\njob = execute(qc, backend, backend_options=backend_options)\njob_result = job.result()\nprint(job_result.get_statevector(qc))\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
